How to install the HDDRIVER demo version:

Boot your system from floppy disk and start HDDRIVER.PRG. Now launch
HDDRUTIL.APP. After double-clicking drive C: HDDRIVER will be installed.
Reboot your Atari in order to activate HDDRIVER.
In order to partition, you select a drive/memory card in the "Devices"
window and then "Partition" in the menu. Partition the medium TOS
compatible and ensure that in the compatibility settings "Byte Swapping"
is disabled.


Important notes:

- TOS cannot boot from SCSI drives that require initiator identification.
With the Atari ST such devices only work with the LINK96/97 host adapters
or the host adapter by Inventronik.
- Most Falcons have problems with their SCSI hardware, especially with high
screen resolutions. Atari proposed several hardware fixes (clock patches).
Because in contrast to other drivers HDDRIVER drives Falcon SCSI with
maximum speed, you might not have noticed this problem before.


Please visit the HDDRIVER website for more information, and for the prices
of the full version and the upgrade conditions:

https://www.hddriver.net
